(warning: I feel rambly after a marathon session of pre-castle prepping.)

Sokoban bores and irritates me, but not as much as Gehennom. I've just 
recently gotten a character that is "ascendable" (almost full kit before 
reaching the castle wand, high HP, very low natural AC) to the point of 
the castle. I then made myself a list of things to do and I looked at 
it... and it looks rather boring.

Probably because I've ascended similar characters quite a few times. 

But then, generally, the beginning bores me, too. I mostly enjoy the mid-
early late game. 

Soko gets really annoying when you've played it enough to memorize the 
maps and you can do them all almost as fast as you can type the 
keystrokes to do it. If I had the know-how, I'd replace Soko with one 
level that had either of the two prizes. If not for the powerful want for 
a BoH or AoR, I'd just pass that right by. (Of course, if I had the know-
how I'd spend a lot of time making the early game less repetitive -- then 
again, 95% of my characters don't make it to the mid-game, so that's 
probably why it's so repetitive.)

I think a good improvement for Soko would be alternative puzzles. Not 
just boulder pushing puzzles. Nethack is so very versatile, I don't see 
why someone with serious coding knowledge couldn't make up a whole slew 
of replacement puzzles.


